Fictional EP Tracklist

Track 1: The Note Refuses the Third Step
- Story & Context: Selin begins with a slow bowed approach toward a neutral third above the drone while Emre holds the same kick-and-bass pattern for thirty-two bars. The tension comes from delay: every time the tanbur appears ready to settle, the bow changes pressure and the pitch bends away by a few cents. Derya answers with prepared-cello strokes whose decay shortens every four bars, while Luca sustains a low recorder tone just above the synth bass, creating a slow beating pattern. At bar thirty-three the tanbur finally reaches the target degree, but the electronic harmony does nothing. The resolution happens entirely in the ear, not in the chord progression. The track ends with one open cello note after the kick has stopped.
- Visual & Lyrics Prompt: Long ferry-maintenance corridor with three painted floor steps, the third partly hidden by shadow, yaylı tanbur bow suspended over a note, mono synth and prepared cello in soft focus. No full lyrics; sparse spoken cues limited to “not yet,” “hold the third,” “closer,” and “leave the grid where it is.”

Track 2: Rosin Opens the Hi-Hat
- Story & Context: Emre maps the envelope of Selin’s bow noise to the level of a narrow hi-hat layer. Soft bowing produces almost no upper percussion; harder pressure gradually reveals a metallic sixteenth-note pattern. Derya plays a two-note prepared-cello ratchet that becomes shorter and drier across the track, while Luca contributes breath-only attacks during every fourth-bar gap. The arrangement feels as if the acoustic friction itself is exposing the electronic machinery. Halfway through, Selin switches to a nearly pure tone and the hats disappear even though the tempo and drum pattern remain unchanged. The final section builds intensity through bow grain rather than added drums.
